}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5{x}_{3},$ and from the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=4$, we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=3,$ $b=20,$ and $c=4.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{20+4}{3}=8.$" 13194139535472 17592186045443 false] [17592186134498 1074 "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5{x}_{3},$ and from the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=4$, we get the vector \n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=3,$ $b=20,$ and $c=4.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{20+4}{3}=8.$" 13194139535472 17592186045443 true] [17592186134499 1071 "Given that $u